    "revision": 1,
    "title": "Write a practical message",
    "subtitle": "An invitation changes · 2",
    "context": "Use the selected vocabulary and constructions to negotiate an invitation and explain a tactful response.",
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "EX-CORE-U3-02-required-composition-produce",
        "kind": "check",
        "title": "Compose a purposeful message",
        "questions": [
          {
            "id": "EX-CORE-U3-02-required-composition-draft",
            "kind": "production",
            "response": "written",
            "prompt": "An invitation changes · 2: Write a practical explanation for someone joining the situation late. State the problem, a supported reason or constraint, and a clear proposed next step.",
            "promptLanguage": "en",
            "context": "妈妈买了一本书，想送给爸爸的一位朋友。她今天要工作，不能一起去，让我和爸爸把书带过去。我以为书是给那位朋友的孩子买的。\n\n妈妈说，他现在在学中文，这本书可以帮他。我说自己也看过，书里的字和我学过的一样。妈妈让我告诉他，有不明白的可以和我们一起看。\n\n到了他家，他的孩子打开门。我没有马上把书给孩子，而是问爸爸的朋友在哪里。孩子说爸爸在里面做饭，让我们先坐一会儿。\n\n爸爸的朋友出来以后，我把书拿给他，说妈妈今天不能来。他很高兴，问我学过哪些字。我给他看我认识的，他也说自己学过的。\n\n回家时，我告诉妈妈，我们没有把书送错，也一起看了一会儿。她笑着说，送东西以前先知道谁需要、为什么需要，比只看谁先开门好。",
            "contextLanguage": "zh",
            "label": "Write your own message",
            "resultDomain": "Self-reviewed writing practice",
            "rubric": [
              {
                "id": "r1",
                "text": "The problem, constraint and next step connect coherently."
              },
              {
                "id": "r2",
                "text": "I distinguished the source facts from my proposal."
              }
            ],
            "minLength": 1
          }
        ],
        "sequential": true
      }
    ],
